node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log
dist/
.vscode-test/
*.vsix
.glyphcompress/

# Secrets — second line of defence.
# The real credential store lives outside this tree (see docs/credentials.md),
# precisely so it cannot be reached by `git add -A`. These patterns exist for the
# case where something lands here anyway: a scratch .env, a token pasted into a
# file during debugging, a key exported by a tool that did not ask.
*.env
.env*
!.env.example
*secret*
*credential*
# ...except the document that explains where the store is. It holds no values,
# and the pattern above catches it by name alone — which is the rule working,
# not a reason to weaken it.
!docs/credentials.md
*.pem
*.key
.glyph-secrets/
